"""Hookii Neomow error / notice codes -> text.

Generated table, one entry per code: (kind, short English label, Hookii's
official English text).

- Codes 101-1076 are the alarm ids the mower firmware can raise (firmware
  1.7.4 alarm table), plus newer ids the Hookii cloud already has texts for
  (e.g. 211-218, 524-537, 615-641, 832-834). Codes 10-24 are account/app
  notices.
- The official text is the one the Hookii app shows: the app downloads its
  notice texts from the Hookii cloud language service
  (``/api/v1/common/app/language/list``) and renders a notice by its
  ``notice_desc_<code>_1`` key. Code 107 has no official text.
- The short label is our own concise wording (used in ``alarm_label``).
  Translations of the short label live in ``translations/<lang>.json``
  under the error binary sensor's ``alarm_code`` attribute states.
- kind: ``fault`` needs attention or stops work, ``warning`` degraded or
  self-recovering, ``info`` a normal status message (e.g. "Charging"),
  ``notice`` an account/app/subscription message. Only fault and warning
  raise the error binary sensor.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

